cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "To cite this formalization, please use the metadata below; for the mathematics, cite the preferred citation."
type: software
title: "Formalization of a counterexample to Vaught's conjecture for L_{ω₁ω}"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof that a sentence of the infinitary logic L_{ω₁ω}, in a countable relational
  language, has exactly ℵ₁ countable models up to isomorphism and no perfect set of pairwise
  non-isomorphic countable models. It is not a counterexample to the first-order Vaught
  conjecture.
